soak-test-reboot: THIS BUILD REBOOTS THE BOARD. It soaks for 120s, then asks for a cold reboot (SBI SRST system_reset, reset type 1) and draws the thread-placement lottery again, forever.
soak-test-reboot: to stop the loop: press any key on this console. The check is a poll of the UART's data-ready bit once every 5s and again 5s before each reset, and the bit is sticky, so a keypress at any moment is found. Stopping disarms the reboot and leaves the soak running; it does not end the run.
soak-test-reboot: the fallback that needs no cooperation from this kernel is the firmware's own autoboot countdown or boot menu on the next boot, and after that, the boot medium.
